<title>BELGIUM: Tractebel H1 EPS up 9.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Tractebel H1 EPS up 9.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>First-half 1996 earnings</p>
<p>(billion Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net (excludes minorities)     7.51 vs     6.81</p>
<p>    Cons earnings/share (francs)	539.6  vs   494.3</p>
<p>Note - Utility group Tractebel said on Monday its net consolidated full-year 1996 earnings should be higher than in 1995, which should allow the group to continue its dividend policy of the past years.  </p>
<p>    Cons turnover			   161.68 vs   151.70</p>
<p>    Cons current gross profit	    25.26 vs    23.14</p>
<p>    Cons current net			 19.94 vs    18.66</p>
<p>    Exceptional profit			0.81 vs     0.27</p>
<p>    Group current net profit		6.65 vs     6.62</p>
<p>Note - Tractebel said results were better in electricity production, communications and real estate. The group said its exceptional earnings included a 975 million franc gain from the flotation of its U.S. unit Sipex.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
